                    "content": "import sys\n\ndef min_layers(N):\n    # For integer points 0..N, all segments [i, j], i < j\n    # Two segments overlap if their interiors intersect.\n    # This is equivalent to interval graph coloring.\n    # The chromatic number equals the maximum number of intervals overlapping at any point.\n    # For integer endpoints, maximum overlap occurs at midpoints like k+0.5.\n    # At point x between k and k+1, intervals covering x are those [i, j] with i <= k and j >= k+1.\n    # Count = (k+1) * (N-k)\n    # We need max over k = 0..N-1 of (k+1)*(N-k).\n    max_overlap = 0\n    for k in range(N):\n        overlap = (k + 1) * (N - k)\n        if overlap > max_overlap:\n            max_overlap = overlap\n    return max_overlap\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    N = int(data)\n    print(min_layers(N))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()",
